            "v": "drugs",
            "ref": "v-drug"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“The squirrels have a good sense of smell,” said their trainer Yin Jin. “Thankfully, we now have better ways of training them.” Once they find drugs in, for example, a box, the animals will use their "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "claws",
            "ref": "v-claw"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to scratch the box."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In China, there are already more than 120 species of sniffer dogs. Why then are we taking the time to train squirrels? It’s partly because they’re smaller than dogs. They grow to about 21 centimetres in length. This allows them to get into tiny spaces easily. What’s more, squirrels can live up to 15 years in "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "captivity"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The six squirrels are now ready to begin work. Wish them all the best in their new job!"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
